## Branch drift

Feature branches may lag `main` on `website/` (missing `HeroDemoArtifact.tsx`, old `Hero.tsx`). If local preview looks wrong:

1. Inspect staged/unstaged/untracked website work and its owner. Compare the specific entrypoint read-only: `git diff main -- website/src/components/Hero.tsx` when that ref exists.
2. Preserve the intended candidate and reconcile only the identified files under the authorized scope. Do not run a blanket `git checkout main -- website/`, subtree restore or branch reset; main may omit newer uncommitted repairs.
3. Restart the isolated preview only after integrating the intended changes; preserve any other agent's shared server.

## Local preview

| Step | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Port | **3001** — `website/package.json` → `"dev": "next dev -p 3001"` |
| URL | `http://localhost:3001` (not 3000) |
| Command | `cd website && npm run dev` |
| Success | Dark home, galaxy hero, **the gap** then logos then quotes. Inner pages stay **light paper** (grid + wash), not flat white. Ask / Change / Indexed on `/product`. |

Never point users at `localhost:3000` for the marketing site unless they explicitly started Next on that port.
